00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:15.834
-For real.
-That's very wild.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:16.868
-It's crazy.
-25 years.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.634
-Clap it up for time.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.434
-I have a photo here.
Look at these guys.

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.000
-Let me see.
-Oh!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.434
-Let's do it.
-You're making the face.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.601
He's got the face. You guys,
he's still got the face.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.067
Come on, he's got the face!
Yeah!

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:34.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.834
And I think it was probably,
like --

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:41.200
I think it was seven years ago,
you came on my show, and we did

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.834
a bit, a reunion, like a little
fun thing of "Good Burger."

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.934
And everyone went nuts.
The Internet went crazy.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:50.434
I think it's up to, like,
30 million views on YouTube.

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.200
-Yes!
-That sounds like a lot.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.267
-That sounds right.
That sounds like a lot.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.534
You guys have a big announcement
to make.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.734
You came exclusively to give it
to us, tonight,

00:00:58.734 --> 00:00:59.734
on "The Tonight Show."

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:00.834
-That's right.
-That's right.

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:01.934
We had to do it here.
Let's do it.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.734
-Kenan, can you tell us
what's going on?

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:07.300
-Um, ladies and gentlemen,
Kel has something

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.267
he'd like to tell you.
-Wow.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.000
All right, here we go.
Kel, whenever you're ready.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.868
-Ladies and gentlemen...
-Oh, wow.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.601
-"Welcome to Good Burger,
home of the Good Burger..."

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:17.868
part two!

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:26.033
♪♪

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.000
-Yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.501
Yo!

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.934
-What!

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.567
Wow.
-Dude!

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:33.634
-What!
-Come on!

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.601
-Come on, baby!
-What?! "Good Burger 2."

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:36.801
-Two!

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:37.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.667
-Yes!

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.467
"Good Burger 2."
"Good Burger 2."

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:46.167
"Good Burger 2!"
Come on, now.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.534
-Oh, man.
-How exciting is this?

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:50.200
-It's a blessing, man.
It's unbelievable.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.634
We're going to shoot it this
summer, and it'll be out soon.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.868
-When -- How did you hear?
How did this --

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.667
This must have been in the works
for a while.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.534
Did it come from this thing?

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:02.033
Did it come from "SNL"?
-I mean, it's been years.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.434
Like, pretty much
since the first one --

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:05.167
-Since the first one,
we wanted to do two.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:06.434
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:08.400
-The crowd, we want it.
The people have spoken.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.267
We want to see this.
-That's right.

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.534
-They have spoken.
-It's happening.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.567
It's happening.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:13.701
-Yes.

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.067
-That's such a big deal.
I'm so excited.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:18.334
So, when you started
on "All That," okay?

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:19.767
You're just straight out
of high school

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.133
or you were in high school?

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.701
-A freshman. 14 years old.
-Barely.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.434
-Sophomore, yeah.
-15.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.701
-And did you know each other
before you got the show?

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:29.133
-We didn't,
and it was funny how we all met.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.334
I don't know if they planned
this, but they had all the kids

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.934
come one by one off the elevator
in the lobby.

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:37.434
And I remember I was down there
already, and the elevator opened

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:40.000
up, and this kid came out
with Mighty Ducks gear on.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.467
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.067
-Wow --
-And he had the roller blades

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:45.300
and everything.
He did the whole like, err!

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.601
And I'm like, "I've got
to hang out with that kid."

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.100
-Wow!
You were wearing the swag?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.701
-I was a very proud Mighty Duck,
yes.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.400
-Yeah, you were a very,
very proud Mighty Duck.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.868
But what made you guys click?

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.400
'Cause sometimes, you don't know
who you're going to click with.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.801
'Cause it's almost like making
a super group, like the Avengers

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.133
of young comedians.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:05.334
-Bro, yeah, I feel like with me
and Kenan, it was just like,

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.334
I would say a joke,
and then he would finish it,

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.400
and it just felt like we gelled
really good.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.434
And then it was in "Mavis and
Clavis" where we figured it out.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.234
-"Mavis and Clavis," dude.
-Yeah, "Mavis and Clavis,"

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.033
yeah, yeah, yeah.
We were playing the two old men.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.400
-For reference, "Mavis and
Clavis" were two old Black men.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.667
[ Laughter ]
And --

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:20.133
-And you were 14 years old?

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.701
-Yeah, 14 years old, kind of,
like, doing the references of,

00:03:23.701 --> 00:03:25.567
like, our dads, uncles,
grandparents.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.901
It was like, "Oh, this guy
is very similar to myself.

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:29.167
I love this dude."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.100
-And did you know
that "Good Burger" clicked

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.701
when you just did that sketch?
And you were like, "Oh."

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.200
-It was a fire sketch
from the beginning.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.434
It was one of the strongest from
like -- it was in the pilot,

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.400
right?
-Yeah, "Good Burger?"

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.834
Oh, yeah.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.234
-Do people still quote you on
"Good Burger" all the time?

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:44.100
-Oh, dude, I get it every day.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.467
Yeah, doesn't matter.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:48.200
Any restaurant that I go to,
could be five star

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.767
or it could be drive through.
they always go,

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:52.100
"Welcome to Good Burger,
home of the Good Burger."

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.033
And I love it.
I get free burgers.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.834
-Yeah, why not.
That's a good gig.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.367
-That's a good gig.

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:58.868
-Is that the only line?
What's the other line?

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:01.601
-Oh, the other one.
Oh, "Who loves orange soda?"

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:04.334
-Yeah.
-"Kel loves orange soda."

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:05.601
-You got that.
-Yep.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:08.734
"I do, I do!"
And then --

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.234
-Very close to home for people
right now.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.300
-Yeah, man.
-Right in the childhood.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.367
-Right in the heart.
-I love it, man.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.767
-Can you tell us what's going to
go down in "Good Burger 2?"

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.901
-Ooh
-Hijinks.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.767
I'd like to say
a lot of hijinks.

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:22.267
-Got to love that.
-Yeah, got to love that.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:25.901
You know, we want, like, as many
cameos as we can possibly get.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.334
Like, anybody that wants to,
like, do it that I guess

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.534
is somewhat famous.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.634
Anyone who's -- there's so many
fans of "Good Burger."

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:36.200
-Yeah. So, like --
-I mean --

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.100
-I want to see what that could
be like.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.334
Could you possibly --
-Could you?

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:40.767
-Come by and do --
-Because we were --

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:41.767
we were talking about it.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:42.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:44.033
-Two, three, four --

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:47.167
♪♪

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:48.701
[ Audience woohoos ]

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.267
-Nice.
-Yeah.

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.367
-Of course, I would do
something-- I would do anything

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.701
with you dudes, anything.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:54.901
Man, I love hanging
with you guys.

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:56.100
-Yes.
-I would love it, man.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.501
I'm excited about this.
-We're very excited.

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:58.901
-So, but there's a script.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.400
You guys are shooting it soon,
by the way.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.701
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:04.367
I think they're waiting on me
to finish upstairs.

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:05.868
-"Saturday Night Live,"
yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.667
Okay, so, any celebrities out
there that want to make cameos,

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.534
clear your schedule
for this summer.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:10.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-Because that's when everyone's

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:11.834
doing it.
-Get ready.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.968
-I also love this song,
"We're All Dudes."

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.300
-Ooh, yeah.
-Yeah, I mean, you wrote that.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.934
-I did write it.
-How did you--

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.100
there's a fun story to this,
right?

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.968
Didn't you write it in like
a night or a day

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.100
or something like that?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.000
I wrote it at a hotel.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.133
Brian Robins was like,
"Hey, we need a song to

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:27.968
the 'Welcome to Good Burger'
that you do on the show."

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:30.734
So, I wrote it really quickly,
and sung it for all the execs,

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.067
and they loved it.
I was, like, at the table,

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.467
and everybody was eating lunch.

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:35.667
And to this day,
I still get paid

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.300
from the "Good Burger" song.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.868
-Exactly right.
That's it, see.

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:42.367
-But it's an uplifting song,
man.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:43.434
It's real uplifting.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.300
-It's the most positive song
there is.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.934
-I love doing it, man.
-Yeah, we never --

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:49.667
We don't ever put anyone on
the spot or force anyone to do

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:51.133
anything...
-What's happening?

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:53.167
What's happening?
-...on this show.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:55.734
